{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations","id":670272,"title":"Awakening Second Edition: Awakened Inspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-18T16:19:46-07:00","id":670272,"title":"Awakening Second Edition: Awakened Inspirations","content":"Could not find the topic on the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/awakened-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">spoiler Blog Post of the same name</a> as I have probably some interesting addition to the inspirations materials for the 2ED.<br /> <br /> <b>Just Remember: <i>It's fan inspirations topic, we probably will not gone in to (almost complete) new corebook.</i><br /> <br /> Notice:</b> For movies and games try to link trailers in posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For start, let's see what Dave had to say on the Inspirations topic over the year ago...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awakened Inspirations</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><b>Comics &amp; Graphic Novels</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Lots of people use film and television metaphors for roleplaying games \u2013 they \u201ccast\u201d their player and Storyteller characters and insert act breaks. I tend to think rpgs are a lot closer to serial comics \u2013 they have a somewhat elastic sense of continuity when they go on too long, and break down into chapters/issues that group into stories which are themselves part of larger arcs.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And the two greatest influences on <b>Mage</b> are comics.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Hellblazer</b> is the original. John Constantine, nicotine-stained, trenchcoated asshole demonologist and mage, has been the character other occult detectives are measured against since he was a side-character in Swamp Thing. His jackdaw magical style fits <b>Awakening</b>\u2018s mages, but it\u2019s his sheer inability to let a mystery go despite the ever-increasing fallout for those around him that really make him stand out. Vertigo are <i>finally</i>collecting the series sequentially, and the volumes released so far cover some of the best stories.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>The Invisibles</b> is the trip. Tonally, it\u2019s closer to <b>Ascension</b> (unless you\u2019re playing a particularly gonzo Chronicle), but the characters and the world they\u2019re in is much, much closer to <b>Awakening</b>: the titular magician-terrorists assign \u201ccabal\u201d roles by symbolism, take on Shadow Names, and fight the forces of universal oppression in a world that\u2019s a hologram between larger, Supernal realities. Its antagonists were a primary inspiration behind the Seers of the Throne; an early arc even has what<b>Mage</b> calls Profane Urim in it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Other comics of potential interest include;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Promethea</b>, an Alan Moore comic about a woman who merges with the Astral incarnation of magic. It features a Tarot- and Kabala-steeped otherworld that\u2019s inspirational for the Astral Realms.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>The Books of Magic</b>, Neil Gaiman\u2019s take on a modern-day mage. Ignore Tim Hunter\u2019s close physical resemblance to another boy wizard (this came first anyway), and take a look at the initial miniseries if nothing else. Among meditations on the nature of magic, mystery, and choice, Gaimain utterly <i>nails</i> Atlantis in a single page.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Locke and Key</b>, by Joe Hill (Stephen King\u2019s son), shows a bereaved family go up against magical family secrets, a house of secrets, and what could easily be an Abyssal entity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Literature</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mage draws on stories about obsession, conspiracy, and the occult.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Umberto Eco is good at dissecting the motivation of mystery-seekers; <b>The Name of the Rose</b> and <b>Foucault\u2019s Pendulum</b> are both appropriate for different reasons.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Weird History fiction of Tim Powers mixes occult research with real events and spins yarns of magic crawling under the world\u2019s skin. The best three books for <b>Awakening</b> are <b>The Anubis Gates</b>, <b>Declare</b>, and <b>Last Call.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The <b>Illuminatus!</b> Trilogy and the <b>Historical Illuminatus</b> by Robert Shea and Bob Wilson mainline the kind of twisting, societies-as-mysteries we\u2019re after for the Orders.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>The Club Dumas</b> by Arturo P\u00e9rez-Reverte shows the main character\u2019s descent through a Mystery Play, and if you read the book instead of watching the movie you aren\u2019t supporting Roman Polanski.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Fight Club</b> by Chuck Palahniuk depicts a particularly violent and strange Thyrsus Awakening. You shouldn\u2019t die without any scars.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Miriam Black trilogy (<b>Blackbird</b>, <b>Mockingbird</b>, and <b>Cormorant</b>) by another Chuck \u2013 former Hunter: The Vigil Developer Chuck Wendig, no less! \u2013 are about a drifter who sees the death of anyone she touches. Violent, sweary, and funny along with the horror.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Clive Barker\u2019s <b>The Great and Secret Show</b> and <b>Imajica</b> show off different facets of Awakening\u2019s world, with rival magicians, layers of reality and \u2013 in Great and Secret Show \u2013 something <i>close </i>to what Awakening means by \u201cAtlantis\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The best book for <b>Awakening</b>, though, for the sheer mood of layers on layers of strangeness, is Mark Z. Danielewski\u2019s <b><span style=\"color:#3366FF\">House</span> of Leaves</b>, at least two layers of which could describe a Mastigos Awakening or Pandemonic Verge. Beware the <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Minotaur</span>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Oh, yes, and there\u2019s that incredibly popular series about a Wizard Detective. <b>The Dresden Files</b> by Jim Butcher aren\u2019t that close to <b>Awakening</b>, being a lot more pulpy, but some of them are quite good and Butcher deliberately follows the narrative beats of mystery fiction in his plotting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Closer to <b>Awakening</b>\u2019s setting are the <b>Night Watch</b> pentology by Sergei Lukyanenko\u2014they\u2019re <i>very</i> Russian, and the first two were adapted into movies you can probably find cheap on an on-demand service somewhere, but they deal with a world with a many-layered magical world underneath, only the shallows of which are accessible. If you need a hand grokking the Fallen / Supernal Worlds, give it a go.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Last, <b>John Dies At The End</b> and its sequel <b>This Book Is Full Of Spiders</b>by David Wong are horror-comedic looks at why you shouldn\u2019t imbue an unprepared Sleeper with Mage Sight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Film</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The film adaptations of <b>Fight Club</b>, <b>Night Watch</b>, <b>John Dies At The End</b>,<b>the Name of the Rose</b>, and Club Dumas (<b>The Ninth Gate</b>) are all worth seeing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Constantine</b> is a frustrating adaptation \u2014 it ignores most of the character of the original, but is surprisingly faithful to the plot beats of the story it\u2019s adapted from (\u201cDangerous Habits\u201d, volume 5 of the current reprint drive, if you\u2019re curious). Ignoring where it came from, it\u2019s a perfectly good modern-occult film, and has one of the best depictions of Mage Sight committed to film.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If Fight Club\u2019s a Thyrsus Awakening, then <b>Donnie Darko</b> is an Acanthus\u2019 mystery play. Caught in a time loop punctuated by his own unjust, random death, a young man starts seeing time. The scene where people\u2019s timelines extrude out of their bodies like silvery threads is pure Acanthus Mage Sight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The non-superhero works of Christopher Nolan are all meditations on obsession in puzzlebox world. There\u2019s something for <b>Awakening</b> in all of them \u2013 a quote from <b>Memento</b> opens Fallen World\u2019s Sleepers Chapter,<b>The Prestige</b> warns of rivalry turned to hubris and murder, and <b>Inception </b>shows what it\u2019s like to invade a victim\u2019s Oneiros.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Of the two gnostic films that came out at the same time (and even shared some sets!) <b>Dark City</b> is more <b>Awakening</b> than <b>The Matrix</b>, if only because the hero has to stay in the prison of the real even after seeing through the Lie he\u2019s been kept in. The Matrix has more flash and catharsis, while Dark City has more heart.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Television</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">There\u2019s a TV adaptation of Hellblazer (again called <b>Constantine</b>) on the way this year, which I await with interest. Let\u2019s hope it\u2019s better than the ill-fated adaptation of the <b>Dresden Files</b>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>True Detective</b> came out of nowhere to be one of the best inspirations for <b>Awakening</b> on the small screen. Rust Cohle is Mastigos as <i>fuck</i>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>The Lost Room</b> deals with the aftermath of reality going <i>wrong</i> in a lonely desert motel room, transforming everything in it into a powerful artifact now sought after by occult conspirators.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Video Games</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The <b>Assassins Creed</b> games feature rival conspiracies (one dedicated to freedom, the other control) astrally-projecting back into history to seek clues to the vanished magical civilization that created humanity and left potent artifacts behind. You can get all kinds of inspiration for <b>Awakening </b>from it, especially if you\u2019re using a historical setting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>The Stanley Parable</b> is short, but is The Lie in a three-hour experience. It\u2019s also very, very funny.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Non-Fiction</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If you\u2019re interested in where Atlantis came from in a modern occult setting, try Joscelyn Godwin\u2019s <b>Atlantis and the Cycles of Time</b>, a survey of the 19<sup>th</sup> and 20<sup>th</sup> century occultist movements <b>Awakening</b>\u2019s cosmology and backstory are based on.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If you want to look at what people <i>really</i> thought about magic in European history, try Stuart Clark\u2019s <b>Thinking With Demons: The Idea of Witchcraft in Early Modern Europe</b>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">If you\u2019re interested in the Supernal World, get your hands on an encyclopedia of symbolism. The original <b>Awakening</b> team recommended <b>The Magician\u2019s Companion: A Practical and Encyclopedic Guide to Magical &amp; Religious Symbolism</b> by Bill Whitcomb.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ken Hite\u2019s <b>Suppressed Transmissions </b>are also an excellent guide to the weird. Ken wrote on Secrets of the Ruined Temple, early in <b>Awakening</b>\u2018s line, and this series (originally written for Steve Jackson Games\u2019 magazine) is worth the difficulty you\u2019ll face in finding it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><b>Music</b></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">By popular demand, I have accepted the challenge from Stew \u201cDJ\u201d Wilson. I always blank when trying to think of the perfect track to go with an individual blog post, so thus far we haven\u2019t had any, but <i>this</i> post is about all media, so I can put an entire playlist up.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cUchAD44xA8&amp;list=PLxNpDUlclGojuynFQkQ5CQf-P27lmncgv\" target=\"_blank\">And here it is</a></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">(Apologies for the last song, by the way. A certain someone bet me I wouldn\u2019t include it. Pay up, Wilson.)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-27-2015, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T16:30:34-07:00","id":670308,"title":"","content":"For starting fan list, I have inspiration I got to seen today:<br /> <br /> <b>Movie - Lucy (2014)</b><br /> <br /> History of very rapid Awakening as Thyrsus for the girl that become drug mule for Taiwan mafia. Great portrayal of new Mage Sight, especially for the Path of Ecstasy and GLORIOUS showing of various Arcana effects. Plus Morgan Freeman is making very interesting speeches about evolution that many Thyrsus could. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only Lucy get lots of Mind dots - but let's see in this chronicle Inferior Arcana idea does not exists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tsR2-v554Hs\" data-code=\"tsR2-v554Hs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tsR2-v554Hs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Book &amp; Television - Johnathan Strange and Mr. Norell </b><br /> <br /> Historical story about XIX century return of Magic to the England after three centuries of no open Awakened works. Most of Diamond mages gone to the colonies after Seers of Throne take over the power on Sleepers in XV century and rest hide very deep under Guardians of Veil supervision. Now, in the times of Napoleonic Wars, two Nameless mages want to return Magic to it's rightful place. Also, very good done crossover with <b>Changeling</b> line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We have dedicated <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/620130-jonathan-strange-mr-norrell-as-awakening-game\">topic only to this series as Awakening chronicle</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iE1nsOoTJos\" data-code=\"iE1nsOoTJos\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iE1nsOoTJos/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T16:56:05-07:00","id":670320,"title":"","content":"Coming up video games...<br /> <br /> <b>Video Game - Rise of Tomb Raider</b><br /> <br /> Finally, game about our famous Sleepwalker Mysterium member archaeologist - Lara Croft - that dwell deep in her Obsession for the uncovering Mystery of Atlantis. Just see this Temples of Time Before to explore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And pesky Sleepers interference in them...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a5V13EqUqO8\" data-code=\"a5V13EqUqO8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/a5V13EqUqO8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Video Game - Assassin's Creed: Syndicate</b><br /> <br /> Whole series is mentioned as general inspiration for gameline, but XIX century London story looks like great source for information about Nameless War. Just see this video of Nameless propaganda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More to talk in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/587806-dark-era-nameless-war\">Nameless War Era's topic</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hTqlsUB1SJE\" data-code=\"hTqlsUB1SJE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/hTqlsUB1SJE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Video Game - Quantum Break</b><br /> <br /> Police detective Awakens as Acanthus and must stop the Cult of Doomsday Clock from destroying the world. Great visualizations of Time Arcanum effects! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ybRB8sBCigw\" data-code=\"ybRB8sBCigw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ybRB8sBCigw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-12-2015, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T02:18:35-07:00","id":670637,"title":"","content":"The Tomb Raider one is interesting because when I first got into Mage, was around the time that that remake of the original game came out. I think that's why I've never really had probems with Atlantis in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T03:27:06-07:00","id":670710,"title":"","content":"Much as I love Strange and Norrell, I really wouldn't use it for Awakening inspiration - between the Lie, Dissonance and Quiescence, Awakened magic just can't have the place in Society that the magic of Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell does.<br /> <br /> I can see it as an idea of what some of the Silver Ladder might <i>like</i> to achieve, and some of the way the magic itself works is great inspiration, but I wouldn't suggest it as a main source for the style of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T03:49:44-07:00","id":670746,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of amused that Awakening's magical paths could be seen as counters to the Laws of Magic from the Dresden Files. Especially if you include the Abyss (Oh, and hello. I've been lurking these forums for a while, and I decided to take the next step and start posting).<br /> <br /> As for inspiration, I probably shouldn't take as much from Escaflowne as I do. Even if a people known as the Draconians are involved, I'm pretty sure Atlantis being a plot point is coincidence. But I imagine Fate spells working like luck enhancement does in this series. Hubris and the irresponsible use of power figure heavily into the storyline, as well. Most of the major characters are guilty of both.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, I kind of have the Acanthus path on the brain. It's tough not to see elements of it Puella Magi Madoka Magica. Fate, Time, Choice and Consequence are definitely there. Though Supernal magic does not cause both hope and sorrow as a rule, it's not a bad mindset for a cautious Mage to have. Even magic worked with the best of intentions can have deadly consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","user":"RdMarquis","date":". 09-19-2015, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","name":"RdMarquis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T00:53:45-07:00","id":675013,"title":"","content":"Two more I think there really should be mentioned in some supplement... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Movie - Doctor Strange: The Sorcerer Supreme</b> <br /> <br /> Animated movie about Awakening of Stephen Strange, Obrimos Arrow, that started when his neuroseurgeon career was ended after car accident. Great showing Adamantine Arrow dogma and what they are in game reality. There are monsters, there is magic, there is philosophy of self improvement. Even half of film takes place in Tibet, where Arrows had Great Caucus in 1945 and reformed their Order. Really, if you never <i>get</i> Arrows just from books ( like me ) just watch it, and everything will click! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Jump to the 1:10 in the clip for proper action <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3IPhA7rbCnk\" data-code=\"3IPhA7rbCnk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3IPhA7rbCnk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Video game -</b> <b>Secret World MMO</b><br /> <br /> A game with <b>very</b> strong plot and climate about world like ours, only that every myth and legend in it are true - and with secret conspiracies fighting over control on the world dwelling in the occult. Sounds familiar? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Secret World is a <b>Mage </b>chronicle with three factions working as representatives of Orders in the story - Templar are Adamantine Arrows, Dragons are Silver Ladder and Illuminati plays a role of Guardians of the Veil ( with a mix of Mysterium ). Beside great backstory and <b>Mage</b> plot ( you fight with modern Necromancer in First Act ), it offers one of best showing of Guardians Labyrinth at work - mainly, Illuminati faction prologue. Just see this below...<br /> <br /> (Jump to the 1:10 in the clip for proper action - before is Seers-like sells pitch that does not have very much to the proper gameplay of Illuminati faction )<br /> <br /> \u200b <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gHvtFoRC2ko\" data-code=\"gHvtFoRC2ko\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gHvtFoRC2ko/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T07:15:27-07:00","id":675206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations#post670272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could not find the topic on the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/awakened-inspirations/&amp;quot;]spoiler</a> Blog Post of the same name[/URL] as I have probably some interesting addition to the inspirations materials for the 2ED.<br /> <br /> <b>Just Remember: <i>It's fan inspirations topic, we probably will not gone in to (almost complete) new corebook.</i><br /> <br /> Notice:</b> For movies and games try to link trailers in posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For start, let's see what Dave had to say on the Inspirations topic over the year ago...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That moment in which i find 14 of my favourites books and films are mentioned as source as one of Mage. God damn, i hadn't thought about the Club Dumas with Mage eyes and now i wonder why. Is perfect. Plus Corso is so Constantine-like in so many ways. <br /> <br /> Get once more time my respect, Dave, sir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T01:25:00-07:00","id":695848,"title":"","content":"The old inspiration I unearthed lately...<br /> <br /> <b>Television - Witchblade</b><br /> <br /> TV series adaptation of comics series about New York police detective Sara Pezzini receives ancient Artifact - the titular <i>Witchblade</i> - that is universal, sentient armor and weapon, bounding with it's wearer and guiding her to fulfilling her great Destiny. Marking this as great show for Acanthus or Adamantine Arrow inspiration is great understatement. Just see below what Witchblade is capable...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRJa9hqJHeY\" data-code=\"gRJa9hqJHeY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gRJa9hqJHeY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, I will not hide this show was one of main inspirations for mine <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/92189-european-knight-legacy?p=95253#post95253\"><b><i>Order of Round Table</i> Legacy</b></a>'s powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T17:49:44-07:00","id":700325,"title":"","content":"Gravity Falls is pretty good inspiration.<br /> <br /> A town that attracts anomalies in reality. Dont wanna spoil anything to people who hadnt watch the show but is a good supernatural mistery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZtlX1pujSr4\" data-code=\"ZtlX1pujSr4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZtlX1pujSr4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Its really inspired me to run a game around Vault III and the horegon vortex (The RL inspiration for the show and an atheneum in mage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-13-2015, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:38:41-07:00","id":714349,"title":"","content":"<b>Movie - Inside Out (2015)</b><br /> <br /> Great showing of child's Onerios, with various goetia working inside it's own dream-scene realm and &quot;governing&quot; the psyche of their host. Did you ever feel that your emotions were tiny people in your head and quarreling how to run your life? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AXGhfYVAOKE\" data-code=\"AXGhfYVAOKE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AXGhfYVAOKE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:44:34-08:00","id":821610,"title":"","content":"Newest inspiration, described as &quot;Harry Potter for Adults&quot;...<br /> <br /> <b>TV - Magicians (2016) </b>( And book series )<br /> <br /> Story about two societies of Awakened - <i>Brakebills University</i>, the Mysterium Academia in Upstate New York. And <i>Hedge Witches coven</i> - Nameless Order cult based in occult underground of NYC proper. Those two groups separate childhood friends, <i>Quentin</i> and <i>Julia</i>, when Quentin pass acceptance test to Brakebills and Julia - not. When he Awakened as Acanthus few months earlier, Quentin was in the severe depression, ending in mental institution. His Awakening show him that his favorite childhood book series were describing real world of magic - <i>Fillory </i>( That in <b>Mage</b> could easily be Arcadia <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - but then Lie hit hard on him and only after joining Brakebills he founds sense in life<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9SuW7c28SAM\" data-code=\"9SuW7c28SAM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9SuW7c28SAM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T21:40:36-08:00","id":823063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=670637#post670637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tomb Raider one is interesting because when I first got into Mage, was around the time that that remake of the original game came out. I think that's why I've never really had probems with Atlantis in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to play Ascenscion and I hard a hard time going across to Awakening. One of the things that sold me on the Awakening version was the Atlantis concept. It made me think of the game as being like Indiana Jones, Tomb Raider or similar, which really drew me into the new mythology. Now I don't really use the Atlantis ideas much at all, but it helped get me excited in the beginning of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:31:23-08:00","id":823657,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>TV - </b><b>The Man in the High Castle</b><b>(2015) </b>( And book )<br /> <br /> Subtle <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> ( and Archmasters ) stuff. Group of Sleepers come in to possession of film that shows alternative version of history ( Aponoia, anyone? ). The so called <i>Man in the High Castle</i> is sending those to show that all last two decades of history world knows is Lie. But does <i>Man </i>really exists in the first place? Plus USA as Nazi-Japan condominium - heaven for Seers of Throne. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hzz_6dmv03I\" data-code=\"hzz_6dmv03I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/hzz_6dmv03I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T06:22:00-08:00","id":828177,"title":"","content":"We lost <b>Constatine</b>, but got the...<br /> <br /> <b>TV - Lucifer (2015)</b><br /> <br /> Series about Mastigos solving criminal cases in modern Los Angeles. He helps with them for Sleeper ( or maybe Sleepwalker? ) police detective <i>Chloe Decker</i>, using his Mind Arcanum power to get the truth from the witnesses. Series rather (very) loosely based on Vertigo comic of the same title, much more lighter in tone than <b>Constantine</b>. Still, great showing of less serious <b>Mage</b> game. Also, interesting is denial in supernatural nature of her partner - is it Dissonance or not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SmuV_Pl4vyc\" data-code=\"SmuV_Pl4vyc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SmuV_Pl4vyc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> BTW: How he makes this thing with the coin using Space only?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-11-2016, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:31:19-08:00","id":828981,"title":"","content":"Other TV pearl I found today...<br /> <br /> <b>TV - Witches of East End ( 2013-2014 )</b><br /> <br /> Story about New England family Beauchamp cabal of four witches, each with her own take on magic, bound by curses of immortality. Character represent four Orders stances - mother Joanna is Mastigos Guardian, protecting her daughters and Mysteries. Aunt Wendy is Thyrsus Silver Ladder, wanting to free the magic, but also cultivate the traditions. Daughter Ingrid is Obrimos Mysterium, wanting to learn all she can about Mysteries. And Daughter Freya is Mastigos of Free Council, rebellious of family, going on her ways about Art.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z1KNqEImlq4\" data-code=\"Z1KNqEImlq4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Z1KNqEImlq4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2016, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:44:02-08:00","id":828989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=828981#post828981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other TV pearl I found today...<br /> <br /> <b>TV - Witches of East End ( 2013-2014 )</b><br /> <br /> Story about New England family Beauchamp cabal of four witches, each with her own take on magic, bound by curses of immortality. Character represent four Orders stances - mother Joanna is Mastigos Guardian, protecting her daughters and Mysteries. Aunt Wendy is Thyrsus Silver Ladder, wanting to free the magic, but also cultivate the traditions. Daughter Ingrid is Obrimos Mysterium, wanting to learn all she can about Mysteries. And Daughter Freya is Mastigos of Free Council, rebellious of family, going on her ways about magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z1KNqEImlq4\" data-code=\"Z1KNqEImlq4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Z1KNqEImlq4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>More like apostates running from their insane Archmaster patriarch from his Lustrum, known as Asgard. They were never born on Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T23:13:37-08:00","id":829143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=828989#post828989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like apostates running from their insane Archmaster patriarch from his Lustrum, known as Asgard. They were never born on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't get them there yet - but story starts with just exploring the magic and the effects on Beauchamp spells and repercusions of their immortality, that is much closer to the normal <b>Mage</b> level. Still, good Archmasters plot twist are also valueable to later in-game exploration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:36:50-08:00","id":832024,"title":"","content":"<b>ERASED / Boku dake ga Inai Machi</b> (2012-2016 manga, 2016 anime)<br /> <br /> Satoru, almost-30ty manga artist, is a man gifted with a weird ability. When something horrible happens in his vicinity, he is kicked back in time to the nearest point from which he could have intervened and stop it; he repeats the loop as long as needed for him to save the day. Satoru is also a man plagued with guilt; as a child, just like many others, he ignored ostracized girl in his classroom. This girl, 15 years ago, fell victim to a serial kidnapper and was murdered, just like 2 other kids from Satoru's school.<br /> While this looks at first like a prelude to a story about solving impossible situations, it's not really about that.<br /> <br /> After spooking a kidnapper by noticing his failed attempt at kidnapping a small girl, Satoru's mother start thinking about the case from 15 years ago. Then, she figures it out! But before she can share it with anyone, Satoru finds her murdered in his home. Desperate to save his mother, he begs for his power to kick in. And it does...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TZzMOC-4k6M\" data-code=\"TZzMOC-4k6M\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TZzMOC-4k6M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zFBmrw8EIMw\" data-code=\"zFBmrw8EIMw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zFBmrw8EIMw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> ...transporting him 15 years back in time.<br /> <br /> While there is pretty much 0 supernatural or magic in the series, other than the central idea of main character being transported back in time, I feel this is a perfect CofD, and more importantly Mage, inspiration. It's pretty dark, touches upon uncomfortable subjects (while still having tact), and it's centered about very creepy mystery. Visuals are good, characters are good, music is good, and writing is good. Manga was fantastic, and while anime has to cut out some of the character scenes due to room limitations (anime is 12 episodes, manga was something about 50 chapters long), it does a superb work so far. I recommend it for everyone, even people not found of typical anime aesthetics and themes. Give it a try! It's a fantastic thriller, even if the central mystery is pretty easy to solve on your own :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 02-17-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T11:39:27-08:00","id":840063,"title":"","content":"Digging this up but I just finished Life is Strange and I must say that if someone wants to make an Acanthus character he/she has to play this game. With it's focus on choices and their consequences, rewinding time and how you can just fuck things up while trying to do the right thing is a very Acanthii thing. Hell, even the town is called <i>Arcadia</i> of all things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:27:11-08:00","id":840175,"title":"","content":"I've been working my way through these and the ones listed in the blog post, and i have to say that True Detective was extremely good. Watching that really hammered home what it would mean to have obsessions instead of aspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:41:33-07:00","id":858737,"title":"","content":"Kristen Britain's <b>Green Rider</b> has a number of alternate Renaissance era scenes that could be adapted (particularly for the Mysterium and Adamantite Arrow). But the scene with the D'yer Wall strikes me as being a quintessential description of the magic of the Tamer of Stones Legacy.<br /> <br /> Some quick background - generations ago, an evil mage twisted the neighboring forest into a place of Lovecraftian nightmares. So the D'yer family sponsored a bunch of stone mages to wall it off.<br /> <br /> Jump ahead a thousand years of so. A new dark mage decides he's going to break the wall, and claim mastery over those dark horrors. So he casually sidles up to the D'yer Wall - unguarded for generations - and tries to blast it with his own magic. After all, he's the student of the Evil Overlord himself! Breaking a wall will be nothing for him!<br /> <br /> Some time later, the dark mage comes to, sprawled out on the grass. And all he can do is stare in shock that <i>humans</i> could make such a thing. Abandoned for centuries, completely untended, and yet he can still hear <i>them</i>. The grunts of the workers, the ringing of hammers, the thud of the stones . . . all woven together into the spells and bound into every inch of the wall. Its been a thousand years, and he can still make out each and every voice, raised together in song. Raising a barrier that no evil could fly over, crawl under, or punch through. A barrier to stand until the end of time, to keep their families safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:02:35-07:00","id":858747,"title":"","content":"It's scattered around, but I found Grant Morrison's take on the New Gods to be pretty apt. Darkseid is basically an Exarch, or the Exarchs are aspects of Darkseid.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://comicsalliance.com/files/2010/09/boss-dark-side.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Him, basically, seen through Mage Sight. The truth behind his words is also shown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T01:25:46-07:00","id":858829,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Out of Sight (\u6572\u6572) </span></b><br /><br /> An animated short that is one of my inspirations for Mage Sight (1E and 2E)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4qCbiCxBd2M\" data-code=\"4qCbiCxBd2M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4qCbiCxBd2M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11537-veloranz","name":"Veloranz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:33:28-07:00","id":863061,"title":"","content":"The parts in <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/Psychonauts\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Psychonauts</b></a> where the protagonist Raz uses his psychic powers to enter the mindscape of some very eccentric people are excellent inspiration for stories focused on exploring Oneiroi. Also, one of the nicknames for the Mastigos in 2ED is Psychonauts, fittingly enough.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/DontRestYourHead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Don't Rest Your Head</b></a> has lots of inspiration for Paradox effects, Abyssals and the parts of the Astral where surreal and psychological horror reigns.<br /> <br /> The entirety of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Film/Eraserhead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Eraserhead</b></a> can be seen as the Mystery Play of a Mastigos. Oppressive industrial landscapes, nightmarish imagery fused with the mundane and an eerie and very sparse soundtrack all come together to give a sense of wanting to escape, to <i>transgress</i>. The fate of the deformed baby at the end can be seen as Spencer signing his name on the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet in a very gruesome way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:32:51-07:00","id":865466,"title":"","content":"EXISTENZ and PI are great films to watch for this, in my opinion. Especially EXISTENZ.<br /> <br /> <b>EXISTENZ</b><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HAdbdUt_h9M\" data-code=\"HAdbdUt_h9M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HAdbdUt_h9M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>PI</b><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jo18VIoR2xU\" data-code=\"jo18VIoR2xU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jo18VIoR2xU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Attached videos. 04-26-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:42:20-07:00","id":865749,"title":"","content":"American Horror Story: Asylum - mental hospital run by Seers of Throne. Sister Jude is mortal who is trying to run catholic asylum overtaken by Seers (sister Mary Eunice and dr Arden). They are prisoning freshly awakened mages (Kit Walker).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1y5Fdz26tuM\" data-code=\"1y5Fdz26tuM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1y5Fdz26tuM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11523-kuaku","name":"kuaku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T07:23:16-07:00","id":865934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kuaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=865749#post865749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">American Horror Story: Asylum - mental hospital run by Seers of Throne. Sister Jude is mortal who is trying to run catholic asylum overtaken by Seers (sister Mary Eunice and dr Arden). They are prisoning freshly awakened mages (Kit Walker).</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything cool, only I would made Arden as the Tremere - his experiments on people does not sound to me very Seer like, rather as Lich Obssesion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:36:51-07:00","id":866089,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that psychological thrillers fit Mage very well. All that existential questioning works for a game where reality is an illusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:31:50-07:00","id":870882,"title":"","content":"Cant believe that no one recommended FATE ZERO and KARA NO KYOUKAI !?<br /> <br /> Everyone can watch FATE ZERO in the Crunchyroll: <a href=\"http://www.crunchyroll.com/fatezero\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.crunchyroll.com/fatezero</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T01:59:08-07:00","id":871060,"title":"","content":"Somebody did, somewhere, that's how I ended up watching that already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T06:53:39-07:00","id":871163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sp4rt01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=870882#post870882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cant believe that no one recommended FATE ZERO and KARA NO KYOUKAI !?<br /> <br /> Everyone can watch FATE ZERO in the Crunchyroll: <a href=\"http://www.crunchyroll.com/fatezero\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.crunchyroll.com/fatezero</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It gets problematic when people try to port stuff from there, though, considering the extreme difference in magical systems. And themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:51:11-07:00","id":871221,"title":"","content":"Bungou Stray Dogs, which is basically about a Cabal of low level Mages (or even Proximi) acting as a official investigators for weird stuff. It's a nice inspiration for cabal dynamics; in 3rd episode, for example, there was an interesting scene where new member of the group tried to guess jobs and occupations of his companions, &quot;from before&quot; joining the Agency. Other's reaction to it (&quot;yeah, every newbie does that, it's a good training I guess&quot;) hit me as something that really could happen in Mage games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T07:33:19-07:00","id":874527,"title":"","content":"Also, no one can tell me that Pippin isn't about Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-BfPfzfX8bI\" data-code=\"-BfPfzfX8bI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-BfPfzfX8bI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:45:04-07:00","id":947433,"title":"","content":"<b>Lock &amp; Key ( comics )</b><br /> Graphic series about family that after tragedy moves in to the old Victorian mansion, shrouded in Mysteries. Unsettling phenomena are starting to come up and past is returning to entwine the future. Good inspiration on how Supernal Magic simply does not stop to work and even centuries after death of mage, his spells can make real horror for Sleepers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Joehilllockekey.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:06:38-07:00","id":947574,"title":"","content":"<b>Fullmetal Alchemist ( 2003 series )</b><br /> <br /> As we are just past premiere of <b>Promethean: The Created</b> 2E we cannot forget great anime that is perfect example of crossover between <b>Mage </b>and <b>Promethean</b>. Elric Brother lose their mother to illness and then themselves when trying to resurrect her \u2013 Edward ends in Moros Awakening where he lose arm and leg. Alfonse, however, almost leaves this world and only will of his brother binds scraps of his conciseness to old armor, creating Homunculus \u2013 this way Al become Unfleshed. From this time brother goes on journey to study ( Supernal ) Alchemy and want to make Alfonse human once again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pwW4e1fl788\" data-code=\"pwW4e1fl788\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pwW4e1fl788/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T02:05:43-07:00","id":947615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=947574#post947574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fullmetal Alchemist ( 2003 series )</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the final antagonist is in my opinion one of the best templates for a Seer I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> Also also, the alchemical circles are great for visualising using High Speech runes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:21:55-07:00","id":947646,"title":"","content":"You know, it just occurred to me that you've missed out the bigger parrallel. The Homunculi are incredibly similiar to Prometheans.<br /> <br /> They have abilities to morph themselves because they're alchemical creations, they're generated by attempts to create life and finally they all have a gnawing awareness that they fundamentally arent' the people they superficially look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:45:23-07:00","id":947654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=947646#post947646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it just occurred to me that you've missed out the bigger parrallel. The Homunculi are incredibly similiar to Prometheans.<br /> <br /> They have abilities to morph themselves because they're alchemical creations, they're generated by attempts to create life and finally they all have a gnawing awareness that they fundamentally arent' the people they superficially look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Series Homunculi are, actually, Sublimati Pandorans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They are 'false created', starts as monsters that become self-aware if they eat enough Philosophical Stone - and still are hungry of more Stone ( i.e. Pyros ). <b>Promethean</b> 2E corebook even goes in to possibility that Sublimati can become proper Created with enough Pyros, that is, in the end, goal of anime's Homunculi.<br /> <br /> P.S. All this talking make me to rewatch original anime from 2003 - of course, as inspiration for my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/825300-cod-mage-magnum-opus-actual-play\"><b>Magnum Opus</b></a> game! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:22:52-07:00","id":963906,"title":"","content":"<b>Mr. Robot ( TV series )</b><br /> Social fearing hacker is joining Free Council extremist column in their fight with Mammon worshiping Seers. He have no idea how much will cost him this revolution... Later on, it dwells also into inner fight with ones Goetia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N6HGuJC--rk\" data-code=\"N6HGuJC--rk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/N6HGuJC--rk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-15-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:15:52-07:00","id":964845,"title":"","content":"If you can get past the initial* storyline, there's a lot to crib from Ken Akamatsu's <b>Negima</b> manga. The protagonist is a young mage, a child-prodigy in the magical arts, sent out on an internship to gain some &quot;real world&quot; experience at a private boarding school. And the series follows him as he makes a series of key life decisions. Picking from one of a half-dozen colorful potential mentors to finish his training. Deciding whether to be a traditional mage (i.e. joining the Mysterium) like his original tutors, or becoming a battle mage (i.e. Adamantite Arrow) like his father. Training his first apprentice. <br /> <br /> What particularly stands out, though, is the &quot;Magia Erebea&quot; arc. To put it in <i>Mage</i> terms, the protagonist is offered a grimoire that will induct him into a (very, very) Left-handed Legacy. And the series does a good job at exploring his dilemma, and the temptations of the Left Hand Path. The protagonist has never wanted to mess with such tainted power . . . but his friends are in terrible danger. And the attainments for Magia Erebea were designed for <i>exactly</i> this sort of situation . . . <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * which is a fusion of <i>Harry Potter </i>meets <i>American Pie</i>, and pretty much screams &quot;author trying to get out of his contract&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:35:05-07:00","id":965051,"title":"","content":"As for Fullmetal Alchemist I'd say Brotherhood is a better watch than the 2003 series. For one it's got a much better main villain, who could be the poster child for Hubris.<br /> <br /> Also now that I think off Madoka Magica is somewhat Mage'y especially in the third movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:04:25-07:00","id":965079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=965051#post965051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one it's got a much better main villain, who could be the poster child for Hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me Dante is pretty much my archetypal of a good Seer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:26:48-07:00","id":965231,"title":"","content":"Dante isn't the villain of Brotherhood, you're talking about the 2003 series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:32:50-07:00","id":966015,"title":"","content":"Their respective series don't work very well for Mage, but my image of the Seers comes from Roman Torchwick (RWBY) and Goffard Gafgarion (Final Fantasy Tactics). Antagonists who are more cynical than cruel, willing to do anything it takes to survive in a dangerous world. They regard their heroic foes as naive and engaged in a pointless struggle that will only lead to problems for everyone around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=965051#post965051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also now that I think off Madoka Magica is somewhat Mage'y especially in the third movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, there's no &quot;somewhat&quot; about it. I think I've mentioned it before, but I see the series as a metaphor for the Acanthus path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","name":"RdMarquis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:21:40-07:00","id":966097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=965231#post965231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dante isn't the villain of Brotherhood, you're talking about the 2003 series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. You were comparing villains of the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:17:00-07:00","id":967552,"title":"","content":"A Silver Ladder lion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukn-IvXHiCw\" data-code=\"Ukn-IvXHiCw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ukn-IvXHiCw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:36:49-07:00","id":967809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=874527#post874527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, no one can tell me that Pippin isn't about Mage: the Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-BfPfzfX8bI\" data-code=\"-BfPfzfX8bI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-BfPfzfX8bI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Months late, but I've been very specifically evoking that scene in my Mage game as an ominous vision of the future, but none of my players are musical theater nerds and my Ben Vereen impression falls on deaf ears <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you want to create a sense of dread and trepidation in your players about attaining mastery/archmastery/some great achievement, don't discourage them from it- encourage them, enthusiastically, loudly, insistently, furiously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T07:55:56-07:00","id":967921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=967809#post967809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Months late, but I've been very specifically evoking that scene in my Mage game as an ominous vision of the future, but none of my players are musical theater nerds and my Ben Vereen impression falls on deaf ears <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you want to create a sense of dread and trepidation in your players about attaining mastery/archmastery/some great achievement, don't discourage them from it- encourage them, enthusiastically, loudly, insistently, furiously.</div> </div> </div> </div>So glad to hear. I've gotten many a person who &quot;didn't like&quot; musical theater&quot; into some of the darker shows like Pippin over the years. Did I introduce you to it, or you've seen it before?<br /> <br /> I also didn't include the first part of the scene, which I think is actually super relevant to the MtAw-ness, but it's also a pretty major spoiler, so I left that part off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:07:23-07:00","id":968328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations?p=967921#post967921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So glad to hear. I've gotten many a person who &amp;quot;didn't like&amp;quot; musical theater&amp;quot; into some of the darker shows like Pippin over the years. Did I introduce you to it, or you've seen it before?<br /> <br /> I also didn't include the first part of the scene, which I think is actually super relevant to the MtAw-ness, but it's also a pretty major spoiler, so I left that part off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a surprising small-world coincidence, I originally saw it years ago and the finale (and the whole Leading Player character) made a big impression on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:43:53-07:00","id":973446,"title":"","content":"The Prisoner.<br /> <br /> Aside from the weird mind-games (which are referenced a good few times in Reign of the Exarchs), it perhaps better than anything I've seen gives an idea of how to portray Seers. You never interact with just a Seer, that person always represents someone above them.<br /> <br /> Also, Rover is totally some kind of spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T20:53:16-08:00","id":1003767,"title":"","content":"Found out great gem of thought food for Mage games! Here I present to you...<br /> <br /> <b>Madame Xanadu ( comic )</b><br /> Great Acanthus and historic stuff for <b>Mage</b> ( i.e. various <b>Dark Eras</b> ) - Her full name was once Nimue Inwudu and she is the youngest sister of Morgana (to become Morgaine Le Fay) and Vivienne, the Lady of the Lake. The sisters are descendants of the Elder Folk, survivors of Atlantis who evolved into the race known as the Homo Magi ( and proper Diamond of gameline ). In the times of Camelot, she was once lover of Merlin , but imprisoned him - for this he stripped her most of her power with last curse. Now she struggle across centuries in helping humans, clashing with other sorcerers and her Obsession over mysterious Fae-like being called Stranger...<br /> <br /> I got very much Silver Ladder vibe from her, even if most of the time she works alone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ( Art design of character is made by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Kaluta#Other_publishers\" target=\"_blank\">Micheal Kaluta</a>, creator of 1E <b>Mage</b> art line we all love! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://art.cafimg.com/images/Category_4569/subcat_8423/xanadu%20cover.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T08:31:48-08:00","id":1009342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/670272-awakening-second-edition-awakened-inspirations#post670272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>Promethea</b>, an Alan Moore comic about a woman who merges with the Astral incarnation of magic. It features a Tarot- and Kabala-steeped otherworld that\u2019s inspirational for the Astral Realms.</span></span></i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Returning to old inspiration from DaveB's list of inspirations...<br /> <br /> <b>Promethea ( Comic )</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tells a story about 'heritage' Person from Astral Space based on Supernal Arcadia that posses next women by centuries. She Awakens them and becomes their Shadow Name. Very interesting play on 'common' Shadow Name Persona. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/tPDuMT9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:33:56-08:00","id":1009412,"title":"","content":"Rhythm of the Heat by Peter Gabrial makes me think of either a Thyrsus or possibly Obrimos Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rzwMe-3XVn4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rzwMe-3XVn4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rzwMe-3XVn4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rzwMe-3XVn4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}